// Computing WCD bounds on a contended node, using residual service curves. 
// Does *not* require the service curve to be *strict*, but requires the flow of interest to have a *minimal* arrival curve. 
// See https://doi.org/10.1109/RTAS61025.2024.00016.

// *maximal* arrival curves for two traffic streams on the same node 
a1 := bucket(2, 2)
a2 := bucket(2, 2)
// *minimal* arrival curve for the flow of interest
a1_min := ratency(1, 1) 
// *(min,+)* service curve offered by the node to the aggregate traffic
sc := ratency(5, 1)
// residual service curve: in this case it is negative
rsc_1 := sc - a2
plot(a1, a1_min, a2, sc, rsc_1)
// per Thm. 19 of the paper, the (possibly negative) residual service curve
// must first be replaced by its lower non-decreasing closure
rsc_1_lc := lowclosure(rsc_1)
// to compute the delay bound, we must use the z-deviation
wcd_1 := zDev(a1_min, rsc_1_lc) \/  hdev(a1, rsc_1_lc)
wcd_1
